Fibonacci(10) = 55
```

## ⚠️ Performance Note

The naive recursive approach has **O(2ⁿ)** time complexity because it recomputes the same subproblems many times. It works well for small values of `n` (roughly up to 40). For larger values, consider:

- **Memoization** (top-down DP) → O(n) time
- **Bottom-up iteration** → O(n) time, O(1) space
- **Matrix exponentiation** → O(log n) time

